## Correction and checks

Summary counts Unicode code points for chunks and the configured truncation
marker. The final cut slices a character array rather than UTF-16 units.
The remaining original algorithm and its declared replacement behavior are
unchanged; no LCS change is included.

The unchanged attacker suite now passes all 27 cases. Nine additional cases
come from direct execution of the original vendored Ruby Summary, including
combining characters, joined emoji, CJK, supplementary deletion and custom
markers. The original diff.rb and summary.rb hashes independently match the
attacker oracle's source hashes. No replacement Ruby algorithm is used.
The extra output is retained in unicode-summary-boundaries.json with its
capture source. The extra assertions also reject generated lone surrogates.

The first save command continued after diff --check flagged CRLF line endings
in both JSON oracle files. The raw bytes were retained locally before their
repository copies were normalized to LF. Deep JSON equality was asserted for
both files; test expectations and captured values are unchanged. The normalized
attacker oracle has SHA-256
8145013d14c7d4061f078a81132c8bc8c16157860c5b5bb894ef77e8ea6db795;
its original raw SHA above remains available in the retained raw copy.
The additional Ruby capture now uses binary stdout so regeneration emits
